{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implemented in worktree ../ac-satisfiability, pushed as Gerrit change 1021 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1021).\n\nPlan review took 3 rounds; both BLOCKs were G1G2 omitted-site findings. The roster-building expression turned out to be duplicated in THREE places (pass1.py:154, fidelity_spot_eval.py:219, eval_solver.py:117), not one — so the fix single-sources it via pass1.build_sibling_roster rather than updating copies. Leaving the two eval harnesses on title-only rosters would have corrupted the dogfooding data G3's deferred posture decision rests on.\n\nLocal gates: make lint clean, make typecheck clean, pytest tests/unit = 5793 passed / 19 skipped / 0 failed. 20 new tests across test_ac_satisfiability_criterion.py and test_container_roster.py.\n\nTwo pinned registries required deliberate updates: test_prompt_front_matter's canonical fixed-point round-trip (front matter canonicalized) and test_threshold_recalibration's full routing-table pin (ac-satisfiability added as advisory 0.95 — the pin exists to catch a silent posture flip). G3's posture/threshold left unchanged per scope."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785380648782873001,"uuid":"89d66743-f885-4d4d-8b49-5dc4d97c9aca"}